ProCaller deployment notes
==========================
Last updated: 13 Oct 2026

Purpose: understand every call route, then deploy ProCaller on a FRESH Ubuntu
server, still using the SAME Synway GSM gateway: SIP peer name gsm222.

Do not take over ViciBox port 80. Ubuntu is a new Asterisk + Django host.
gsm222 stays the PSTN/SIM path (today it lives on / is reachable as the
existing Synway gateway used by ViciBox).


1. What ProCaller is (calling stack)
------------------------------------
Browser Dialer (React + sip.js WebRTC)
  -> registers as SIP phone 2100 / 2101 / 2102
  -> INVITEs either a 10-digit mobile OR a conference room pc{sessionId}

Django (Daphne / ASGI)
  -> stores Call rows, wrap-up, dispositions, recordings ACL
  -> ARI  HTTP  :8088  originate / hangup customer legs (ratio > 1)
  -> AMI  TCP   :5038  backup originate + hangup

Asterisk
  -> WebRTC SIP for agents
  -> Dial(SIP/gsm222/<10digit>) to the Synway GSM gateway
  -> ConfBridge for dial-ratio 2-32 (first answer wins)

.env switch:
  TELEPHONY_BACKEND=asterisk   # real calls
  TELEPHONY_BACKEND=sandbox    # fake ring/answer, no Asterisk


2. Same gsm222 gateway (locked decision)
----------------------------------------
We KEEP using Synway trunk name: gsm222

Today on ViciBox that peer is chan_sip:
  Dial(SIP/gsm222/${EXTEN})

On Ubuntu Asterisk (PJSIP preferred) map the same gateway:
  Option A (simplest if gateway is chan_sip compatible):
    Dial(SIP/gsm222/${EXTEN})
    and keep a chan_sip peer [gsm222] pointing at the Synway IP.

  Option B (clean Ubuntu):
    PJSIP endpoint gsm222 (identify by IP of Synway)
    Dial(PJSIP/${EXTEN}@gsm222)

Either way the DESTINATION is the same hardware gateway. Do not buy a new
ITSP for phase 1.

What you MUST know about gsm222:
  - It is typically 1 SIM / 1 concurrent PSTN call unless the chassis has
    more ports. Dial ratio 4 will try 4 mobiles at once; extra legs will
    fail or queue on the gateway. Ratio 1 is the safe default until we
    confirm how many GSM ports exist.
  - Agent WebRTC and customer GSM audio both mix in Asterisk. The gateway
    only sees the customer leg.
  - Django ARI "watch_gateway" currently looks for the string "gsm222" in
    the Asterisk channel name. Keep that name so ringing/answer detection
    keeps working.


3. Two call routes (do not mix them up)
---------------------------------------

ROUTE 1 — Manual, and Preview Auto with ratio = 1
  "Client dial"  (this is the proven 1:1 path)

  1. Browser POST /api/telephony/session/
     Django returns:
       sip uri      sip:2101@<asterisk-ip>
       password     2101 (or user.sip_password)
       ws_url       ws://<asterisk-ip>:8088/ws
       conference   pc{session.id}   (not used on ratio 1)

  2. sip.js registers over WebSocket.

  3. Agent presses Call.
     POST /api/calls/  { phone, client_dial: true }
     Django ONLY creates the Call row. Asterisk is NOT originated by Django.

  4. Browser INVITE sip:<10digit>@<asterisk-ip>
     extra header: X-ProCaller-Call-Id: <call.id>

  5. Dialplan context [procaller-agent], pattern _X.
       Progress()
       Answer()          ; WebRTC DTLS up first so agent hears in-band ring
       MixMonitor pc-<id>.wav
       Dial(SIP/gsm222/${EXTEN},60,tTo)

  6. Ringing: browser reports POST /api/calls/<id>/ringing/
     Django also polls ARI for a channel whose name contains gsm222.

  7. Customer answers: talk path is
       mic <-> WebRTC <-> Asterisk <-> SIP/gsm222 <-> SIM

  8. Hangup: browser BYE + POST /api/calls/<id>/hangup/
     Browser also uploads its own WebM recording to Django.

ROUTE 2 — Preview Auto with ratio 2..32
  "Server originate into conference"

  1. POST /api/calls/preview-batch/  { campaign_id, ratio }
     Django reserves N distinct leads, same dial_batch id.

  2. For each number Django ARI POST /ari/channels
     TODAY (ViciBox only):
       endpoint = Local/331<10digit>@default
       then when that answers, drop into context procaller-agent
       extension = pc{session.id}  (ConfBridge)

     UBUNTU MUST CHANGE THIS:
       Do NOT use Local/331...@default  (that is a VICIdial trick).
       Originate straight to gsm222 then into conference:
         endpoint = SIP/gsm222/<10digit>
         or PJSIP/<10digit>@gsm222
         app/context = procaller-agent / pc{session.id}

  3. Browser INVITE sip:pc{session.id}@<asterisk-ip>
     Dialplan [procaller-agent] _pc. -> ConfBridge(${EXTEN},procaller_bridge,procaller_user)

  4. First gsm222 leg that goes UP = winner.
     Django drop_parallel_legs() hangs up the other ARI channels.

  5. Agent hears only the winner in the conference.


4. Asterisk objects ProCaller expects
-------------------------------------
SIP / PJSIP WebRTC agents (from backend/asterisk/sip_procaller.conf
and pjsip_procaller.conf):
  2100 secret 2100   (super admin demo)
  2101 secret 2101   (agent demo)
  2102 secret 2102
  context = procaller-agent
  webrtc / DTLS / ICE / ulaw+alaw  (opus optional)
  cert: /etc/asterisk/keys/procaller.pem

Contexts (backend/asterisk/extensions_procaller.conf):
  [procaller-agent]
    _pc.   -> ConfBridge
    _X.    -> Dial gsm222   (manual / ratio 1)

  [procaller-outbound]
    _21XX  -> Dial SIP/${EXTEN}     (internal WebRTC)
    _1XXX  -> Dial SIP/${EXTEN}     (legacy VICIdial phones; skip on Ubuntu)
    _X.    -> Dial gsm222

ConfBridge (backend/asterisk/confbridge_procaller.conf):
  [procaller_user]  [procaller_bridge]
  quiet, no join/leave sounds

ARI user (backend/asterisk/ari_procaller.conf):
  [procaller]  password ProCallerAmi0478  (change on Ubuntu)

AMI user (backend/asterisk/manager_procaller.conf):
  [procaller]  secret ProCallerAmi0478
  permit 127.0.0.1 and 192.168.0.0/16
  originate permission required

Hold music is NOT in Asterisk. Browser mixes campaign MP3 onto WebRTC.
Listen/whisper/barge is logged only; ChanSpy is not live yet.


5. Django .env for Ubuntu + same gsm222
---------------------------------------
Put Django on the Ubuntu box (or on LAN talking to Ubuntu Asterisk).

TELEPHONY_BACKEND=asterisk
ASTERISK_ARI_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8088
ASTERISK_ARI_USER=procaller
ASTERISK_ARI_PASSWORD=<new-secret>
ASTERISK_ARI_APP=procaller
ASTERISK_AMI_HOST=127.0.0.1
ASTERISK_AMI_PORT=5038
ASTERISK_AMI_USER=procaller
ASTERISK_AMI_SECRET=<same-secret>
ASTERISK_SIP_WS=ws://<ubuntu-lan-or-public-ip>:8088/ws
ASTERISK_SIP_DOMAIN=<same-ip-or-hostname>
ASTERISK_TRUNK=gsm222
ASTERISK_STRIP_COUNTRY_CODE=91

Browser MUST reach ASTERISK_SIP_WS and RTP. AMI/ARI can stay localhost
if Django is on the same Ubuntu machine.

If Django stays on another PC (Windows office PC), point ARI/AMI at the
Ubuntu LAN IP, and still keep AMI/ARI off the public internet.


6. Ports on Ubuntu Asterisk
---------------------------
  5060/udp     SIP signaling to gsm222 (and optional UDP phones)
  8088/tcp     ARI HTTP + SIP WebSocket /ws
  5038/tcp     AMI  (LAN only, never on the router)
  10000-20000/udp   RTP (WebRTC + gsm222)
  8000/tcp     Django API (Daphne)  LAN or behind nginx
  80/443       nginx UI  (only if this Ubuntu box is the website;
               do not steal ViciBox :80)

Router: do NOT forward 5038 or 5432. Forward 80/443 only if the public
site is this Ubuntu box. WebRTC from the internet also needs 8088 and RTP
unless you put nginx TLS in front of WS (wss).


7. Ubuntu install order (when deploying)
----------------------------------------
Fresh Ubuntu 22.04/24.04. Do not install VICIdial.

A. OS packages
   asterisk  (distro or compiled 18/20)
   postgresql
   python3.12 + venv, nginx, nodejs 20 (to build frontend once)
   openssl  (DTLS cert)

B. Copy this repo to /opt/procaller_2026
   (project folder name = procaller_2026)

C. Asterisk config (from backend/asterisk/)
   - Generate /etc/asterisk/keys/procaller.pem
   - Include sip_procaller.conf OR convert agents to pjsip_procaller.conf
   - Include extensions_procaller.conf in extensions.conf
   - Include confbridge_procaller.conf
   - Enable http.conf (enabled=yes, bindaddr=0.0.0.0, tls optional)
   - Enable ari.conf + include ari_procaller.conf
   - Enable manager.conf + include manager_procaller.conf
   - CREATE peer/endpoint gsm222 pointing at the SAME Synway IP/port
     the ViciBox box uses today. Copy host, username, secret, codecs
     (usually ulaw/alaw) from the live sip.conf [gsm222] on 192.168.1.200
   - Change Dial() targets if using PJSIP:
       Dial(PJSIP/${EXTEN}@gsm222,60,tTo)
   - Change Django ari_client.originate_to_conference() off Local/331@default
     to SIP/gsm222/<number> or PJSIP/<number>@gsm222
   - asterisk -rx "core reload"  then
     asterisk -rx "sip show peer gsm222"  (or pjsip show endpoint gsm222)

D. PostgreSQL
   CREATE USER / DATABASE procaller
   Django DATABASE_URL=postgres://...

E. Django
   venv, pip install -r backend/requirements.txt
   migrate, seed_demo
   systemd: daphne -b 127.0.0.1 -p 8000 procaller.asgi:application

F. Frontend
   npm run build
   nginx serves frontend/dist
   proxy /api /admin /media /ws -> 127.0.0.1:8000

G. Prove Route 1 BEFORE Route 2
   1. Agent login agent@apinfotech.com  (demo password from seed)
   2. Dialer Manual, call a real mobile
   3. Confirm gsm222 channel in "core show channels"
   4. Then try Preview Auto ratio 1
   5. Only then enable ratio 2 (remember: one SIM = one live customer)


